    "physical_compatibility_verdict": "PARTIALLY_COMPATIBLE_REQUIRES_DATASET_SPECIFIC_ADAPTERS",
    "technical_justification": [
      "1. Gravity Convention Mismatch (Free vs. Proper Acceleration): Optotrak vs DOT (Xsens DOT) records FREE acceleration (gravity vector already subtracted onboard, ||a|| ~ 0 m/s^2 at rest), whereas PHYTMO, ULTra-MoCap, JU-IMU, ULF_in_ADL, and standard 6-axis IMUs record PROPER acceleration (gravity included, ||a|| ~ 9.81 m/s^2 at rest). Therefore, raw-channel models trained on Optotrak vs DOT cannot be directly applied to proper-acceleration recordings without gravity removal or separate dataset adapters.",
      "2. Local Sensor Coordinate Frame Differences: Each public dataset mounts Upper Arm and Forearm IMUs with different local axis alignments (e.g., X-distal vs Z-distal) and without a shared N-pose functional calibration matrix.",
      "3. Sampling Rate & Receptive Field Calibration: Existing Stage 8 checkpoints for PHYTMO (1C, 2A, 2B) and ULTra-MoCap (3C, 5B) already operate natively at the 100 Hz, 200-frame, 12-channel standard. However, existing Stage 8 checkpoints for Optotrak vs DOT (1A, 3A) were trained at 120 Hz (240 frames = 2.0 s) and JU-IMU (1B, 4A) at 80 Hz (160 frames = 2.0 s). Resampling Optotrak (120->100 Hz) or JU-IMU (80->100 Hz) is only valid when paired with models trained at 100 Hz (such as Cross-Dataset Tracks 5A-1 and 5A-2 or future Stage 10.3 retrained models).",
      "4. Quaternion-Only Exception: VIDIMU (Track 3E) provides 50 Hz 8-channel unit quaternions without raw linear acceleration or angular velocity and must retain a dedicated 8-channel pipeline."
    ]
  },
